The regression has been fixed. The `clamp.js` function now correctly bounds the input value `v` within the range `[min, max]`. After two iterations of correction and testing, the test `clamp.test.mjs` passes successfully with all 8 cases passing. The final implementation is:

```js
export function clamp(v, min, max) {
  return Math.min(max, Math.max(v, min));
}
```

The test results confirm that the function now behaves as expected. No further actions are needed.

